 "notes": [
  "openings are Envisat-era inversions exactly as provided (no uncertainties; different regularization and greens functions from the 2026 fit)",
  "the epoch-file row order follows plot_3d_dyke_only.dat, confirmed by Ian Hamling's own plotting script doplot3d.m (provided 2026-09-17), which indexes an opening file by the geometry file's row number",
  "the delivered sept05 file is the raw inversion regridded to 20 km (Ian Hamling, 2026-09-17): it integrates to 3.55 km3 against the published ~2.5 km3 and its deep opening (up to 12.9 m at 16-17 km; 1.74 km3 below 10 km) is ill-constrained, so the figure shows the upper 10 km and like-for-like comparisons quote the above-10-km column; his updated 10-km model (sept05_updated_model) is decoded per his 2026-09-17 layout note \u2014 dyke section lines 171-920, 10 one-km rows per column at the same 75 horizontal positions, the trimmed ends fault sections \u2014 and drawn as the September 2005 panel",
  "the updated model shifts opening toward the NW relative to the raw field's upper 10 km because the raw below-10-km opening is NW-weighted and the 10-km inversion carries that moment in shallow patches; sept05_along_strike records the volume centroids",
  "the delivery has 15 post-2005 files against the 13 published post-megadike intrusions; Ian Hamling's 2026-09-17 update lists the canonical 13 (keep july09 and may10, drop the defunct june09 and apr10), matching the data-derived version pairs (may10 is apr10 with cells below 0.5 m removed; july09's positive cells all lie inside june09's at r=0.994, all other pairs |r|<=0.44); the alternatives record the superseded selection and the untrimmed-apr10 variant",
  "every post-2005 file carries a positive floor of 0.29-0.72 m, consistent with the papers' discard of opening below the local 2-sigma uncertainty (typically 0.3-0.4 m; only may10's 0.5-m cut is proven exactly, against apr10), while sept05 is unfiltered (cells down to 4e-4 m) and the 2026 totals keep all fitted opening; the volume_at_0p5m_floor_km3 values apply one uniform 0.5-m floor to the primary cumulative and to 2026 as a sensitivity, not as a matched reconstruction of any delivered filtering",
  "the shared s axis compares openings by along-axis position; the two traces differ by up to 1412 m mid-plane"
 ],
